But to your first point, what are the individuals on a team? Players? How would you describe a non-pro sporty type? Like someone who swims a lot or plays football at the park.

@Xword Junkie
Need a word for "female CODGER" I guess...

OLD YELLER...wonderful book.  I read it aloud to my students (HS and Jr High)--an incentive to work at improving reading skills:  worth it!  It was a chapter a day until near the end; no way could I stop after the boy calls Old Yeller down to the campfire and shoots him.  I always continued through the final chapter...gave those big tough guys a chance to blink back the tears.

@Mean Old Lady
This week I finally learned what grits are. An unknown food in the UK, watching My Cousin Vinny with youngest son completed my education of Southern cuisine. 
Ah, Marisa Tomei ‘The Defense is wrooowang’ So sweet.

@Heidi
I had headboy for a while too. Took a few crosses to convince me to give up on it.
I just kept remembering "I'm headboy, step aside!" or whatever the one Weasly brother kept saying 🤪

@Amy et al

I would have thought Corvair got some kind of recognition....

(ducking and running)

@Amy

First car I got to drive regularly was my mom's '65 Mustang, which she got just after I turned 16. It wasn't until years later that it dawned on me that she had almost certainly gotten that just for me. 

....

@Amy
My first car was a '73 Dodge Dart. What I remember most was that I could see all four corners when parking. With today's rounded hoods and trunks, I can't ever tell where I'm at. Thank goodness for back-up cameras.

High school were family cars starting with a VW Beetle. For college, the verdict was that I could make do with a bicycle because my dad had, on the same campus. I was not happy.

